<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="NCII Privacy Policy - Privacy and protection against non-consensual intimate imagery.">
  <title>NCII Privacy Policy</title>

  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f6f7fb;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --text: #1f2937;
      --muted: #6b7280;
      --primary: #4f46e5;
      --border: #e5e7eb;
      --danger: #b91c1c;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    header {
      background: var(--primary);
      color: white;
      padding: 48px 20px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    header h1 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: 2.2rem;
    }

    header p {
      margin: 0;
      opacity: 0.9;
    }

    main {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 0 20px;
    }

    section {
      background: var(--card);
      padding: 28px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 0;
      color: #111827;
    }

    h3 {
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .notice {
      border-left: 4px solid var(--danger);
      background: #fef2f2;
      padding: 16px;
      margin: 20px 0;
    }

    ul {
      padding-left: 24px;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--primary);
    }

    footer {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 30px 20px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .updated {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <header>
    <h1>NCII Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Privacy, safety, and protection from non-consensual intimate imagery</p>
  </header>

  <main>

    <section>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: August 20, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>ViralMMSVideo</strong>
        handles personal information and reports involving non-consensual intimate imagery
        (NCII).
      </p>

      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Important:</strong>
        We do not permit the creation, upload, distribution, sharing, or promotion of
        intimate images or videos without the consent of the person depicted.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>1. What Is NCII?</h2>

      <p>
        Non-consensual intimate imagery (NCII), sometimes referred to as
        intimate-image abuse, is intimate or sexually explicit content shared,
        published, or distributed without the consent of the person depicted.
      </p>

      <p>
        This may include photographs, videos, manipulated or altered media,
        or other intimate content where the person has not consented to its
        distribution.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Our Privacy Principles</h2>

      <p>We aim to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Protect the privacy and dignity of individuals.</li>
        <li>Prevent the distribution of NCII through our services.</li>
        <li>Handle reports confidentially where reasonably possible.</li>
        <li>Collect only information reasonably necessary to investigate reports.</li>
        <li>Restrict access to sensitive information to authorized personnel.</li>
        <li>Take appropriate action when content violates our policies or applicable law.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Information We May Collect</h2>

      <p>
        When you submit an NCII report, we may collect information necessary
        to review and respond to the report, such as:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Your name or contact information, if you choose to provide it.</li>
        <li>Information about the reported content.</li>
        <li>URLs or other references identifying the content.</li>
        <li>The reason for your report.</li>
        <li>Information needed to verify ownership, identity, or consent when appropriate.</li>
        <li>Technical information associated with the submission, such as timestamps and security logs.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        You should avoid submitting unnecessary sensitive personal information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. How We Use Report Information</h2>

      <p>Information submitted in an NCII report may be used to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Review and investigate the report.</li>
        <li>Identify and remove prohibited content.</li>
        <li>Prevent repeated abuse or re-uploading of prohibited material.</li>
        <li>Communicate with the reporter when necessary.</li>
        <li>Protect users and the security of our services.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations and valid legal requests.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Confidentiality</h2>

      <p>
        We treat NCII reports and related information as sensitive. Access is
        limited to personnel or service providers who need the information to
        perform legitimate safety, security, moderation, legal, or support
        functions.
      </p>

      <p>
        We may disclose information when required by law, necessary to respond
        to a valid legal process, or reasonably necessary to protect users,
        prevent abuse, or protect our rights and services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Removal Requests</h2>

      <p>
        If intimate imagery depicting you has been shared without your consent,
        you may submit a removal request through our designated reporting
        process.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>NCII reporting:</strong>
        <a href="[NCII_REPORT_URL]">Submit an NCII Removal Request</a>
      </p>

      <p>
        Please provide enough information for us to locate the material.
        Do not send additional intimate material unless it is specifically
        required by the reporting process.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>

      <p>
        We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the
        purposes described in this policy, including investigation, abuse
        prevention, security, dispute resolution, and legal compliance.
      </p>

      <p>
        Retention periods may vary depending on the nature of the report,
        applicable law, and legitimate safety or security requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Security</h2>

      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational
        safeguards designed to protect sensitive information from unauthorized
        access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.
      </p>

      <p>
        No online service can guarantee absolute security, but we continuously
        work to reduce risks associated with sensitive information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

      <p>
        Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights
        relating to your personal information, including rights to access,
        correction, deletion, restriction, or objection to certain processing.
      </p>

      <p>
        To exercise an applicable privacy right, contact us using the details
        below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Children and Minors</h2>

      <p>
        We take reports involving minors extremely seriously. Content depicting
        or appearing to depict a minor in sexual or exploitative circumstances
        may be subject to additional legal and safety procedures.
      </p>

      <p>
        Do not upload, forward, or otherwise distribute suspected child sexual
        abuse material. Use the appropriate reporting channels available in
        your jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Third-Party Services</h2>

      <p>
        We may use trusted service providers for hosting, security, abuse
        prevention, customer support, and other operational purposes. Such
        providers may process information only as necessary to provide their
        services and subject to appropriate contractual or legal safeguards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>

      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make
        material changes, we may update the date shown at the top of this page
        and provide additional notice where required.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>

      <p>
        For privacy questions, NCII removal requests, or concerns about the
        handling of personal information, contact:
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>ViralMMSVideo</strong><br>
        Privacy Team<br>
        Email:
        <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY_EMAIL]">[PRIVACY_EMAIL]</a>
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer>
    &copy; 2026 ViralMMSVideo. All rights reserved.
  </footer>

</body>
</html>